$$\begin{align*}
P&=x+(x+3)+(x+4)\\
P&=3(1+2\sqrt{2})+7\\
P&=10+6\sqrt{2}
\end{align*}$$
The perpendicular sides are $x$ and $x+3$:
$$\begin{align*}
A&=\frac12x(x+3)\\
A&=\frac12(1+2\sqrt{2})(4+2\sqrt{2})\\
A&=\frac12(12+10\sqrt{2})\\
A&=6+5\sqrt{2}
\end{align*}$$

